PROJECT OVERVIEW

We are looking for a talented architect, hospitality designer or interior/exterior designer to develop a complete visual restyling for an existing outdoor food, drink and events venue located in Western Sicily, Italy.

This is not a new construction or a complete landscape redesign.

The venue already has mature plants, large trees, palm trees, vineyard rows, rustic wooden benches, existing seating areas, an operational kiosk/bar and a bathroom. These existing features should be preserved and enhanced.

The goal is to create a coherent, elegant and highly recognisable Mediterranean identity by improving the existing exterior spaces and redesigning the interior of the kiosk/bar and bathroom.

DESIGN DIRECTION

The desired atmosphere should be:

* contemporary Mediterranean;
* natural, warm and atmospheric;
* elegant but informal;
* authentic and connected to Sicily;
* highly photogenic and suitable for social media;
* attractive during the daytime, at sunset and at night.

Preferred materials and visual elements include terracotta, natural stone, textured plaster, raw or aged wood, woven fibres, rattan, linen, rope, dried palm leaves, olive and vine branches, earthy colours and warm ambient lighting.

The final result must not look tropical, excessively bohemian, artificial or like a stereotypical rustic restaurant. We want a refined and emotionally engaging Mediterranean environment.

REFERENCE IMAGES

We will provide reference images showing the general style and some desired elements. These images are for inspiration only and should not be copied literally.

The selected designer must interpret the references and adapt them to the real venue, its existing vegetation, vineyard setting, operational requirements and available budget.

SCOPE OF WORK

1. EXTERIOR RESTYLING

The existing plants, vineyard rows, trees and wooden benches must remain.

The designer should study how to improve, style or reposition the existing elements and create a coherent visual experience throughout the venue.

Elements and areas to be developed may include:

* styling of the existing wooden benches using outdoor rugs, cushions, fabrics and small tables;
* comfortable lounge areas with large cushions and low seating;
* a conversation-pit-style lounge area, preferably achievable without major excavation;
* groups of large terracotta jars, amphorae and pots in different sizes;
* curated Mediterranean still-life installations and decorative vignettes;
* compositions using terracotta, woven baskets, natural stone, raw wood, olive branches, vine branches, dried natural elements, candles and seasonal fruit;
* a compact sculptural fountain or water feature with a natural stone or textured finish;
* a natural stone or textured wall incorporating safe candle lighting;
* large decorative mirrors, possibly framed with natural fibres or dried palm leaves;
* one main Instagrammable photo spot that feels original and connected to the venue;
* secondary photographic corners distributed throughout the space;
* outdoor fabric canopies or draped textile installations where appropriate;
* woven rattan or natural-fibre pendant lights and artistic lighting compositions;
* improvement of the external appearance of the kiosk/bar;
* entrance styling and discreet signage;
* warm evening lighting for paths, trees, vineyard rows, benches and decorative features.

All outdoor materials must be suitable for a coastal Mediterranean climate and resistant to sun, wind, humidity and salt exposure.

The designer is not required to include every element mechanically. We expect professional judgement to determine what should be used, where it should be placed and what should be avoided.

2. KIOSK/BAR INTERIOR DESIGN

The small existing kiosk/bar requires a complete interior visual restyling while maintaining its operational function.

The project should study:

* overall colour palette and material selection;
* wall and ceiling finishes;
* bar-counter front and worktop finishes;
* back-bar design;
* shelves, bottle display and decorative storage;
* warm functional and ambient lighting;
* menu and signage placement;
* storage solutions;
* small decorative details;
* integration of terracotta, natural stone, wood and woven materials;
* possible improvement of the kiosk’s exterior cladding.

The design must be attractive but also practical for daily bar and food-service operations.

3. BATHROOM RESTYLING

The bathroom should follow the same Mediterranean identity.

We would like the designer to explore:

* a terracotta jar or sculptural natural-stone washbasin;
* a distinctive wall-mounted tap;
* a large round or organically shaped backlit mirror;
* textured walls or natural plaster;
* warm indirect lighting;
* simple shelves and practical accessories;
* decorative details consistent with the rest of the venue.

The bathroom design must remain hygienic, durable, easy to clean and technically feasible.

REQUIRED DELIVERABLES

The final project should include:

* analysis of the existing venue based on photographs, measurements, plans and video;
* one complete design concept;
* moodboard and visual identity;
* colour and material palette;
* annotated 2D layout showing the placement of all proposed elements;
* design of the main exterior areas;
* interior design of the kiosk/bar;
* bathroom design;
* photomontages using photographs of the real venue where useful;
* realistic 3D renderings in both daytime and nighttime conditions;
* at least 8–12 final views covering the principal areas;
* drawings with basic dimensions for custom-made elements;
* lighting, material and colour specifications;
* shopping list with real products or equivalent specifications;
* preference for products available in Italy or within the European Union;
* suggestions divided into essential, recommended and optional items;
* preliminary cost estimate or budget ranges for the proposed solutions;
* practical instructions that can be given to local craftsmen;
* at least two revision rounds;
* final presentation in PDF format;
* editable/source files used to produce the project.

REMOTE WORKFLOW

The project can be completed entirely remotely.

We can provide:

* detailed photographs of the existing venue;
* measurements and available plans;
* daytime and nighttime videos;
* video calls and a live virtual tour;
* additional photographs requested by the designer;
* drone images if required.

Professionals who are available to visit Western Sicily may also apply. Any proposed site visit and travel expenses must be quoted separately and must not be included automatically in the initial bid.

IDEAL CANDIDATE

We are looking for someone with proven experience in at least one of the following areas:

* restaurant, bar or café design;
* outdoor hospitality design;
* boutique hotel or resort design;
* Mediterranean interior design;
* exterior styling;
* 3D architectural visualisation;
* commercial space planning.

The candidate must be capable of developing the actual design, not only producing attractive renderings based on instructions provided by us.

Generic AI-generated images without accurate space planning, measurements, material research and real implementation details will not be accepted. AI may be used as part of the creative process, but the final project must be based on the actual venue and must be realistically buildable.

HOW TO APPLY

Please include the following information in your proposal:

1. Three relevant portfolio examples, preferably involving hospitality or outdoor venues.
2. A short explanation of how you would approach an existing venue without removing its current natural features.
3. Confirmation that you can provide both exterior design and kiosk/bar interior design.
4. Confirmation that you can provide daytime and nighttime renderings.
5. Confirmation that you can provide a shopping list and practical indications for local craftsmen.
6. Your proposed fixed price.
7. Estimated delivery time.
8. Number of revisions included.
9. Whether you are available for an initial video call.
10. Whether you could potentially visit Western Sicily and the separate cost of doing so.

Please begin your proposal with the words “MEDITERRANEAN RESTYLING” so we know that you have read the full description.

